      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "IV-domain-and-precision",
          "source": "PDF40 / printed39 first instruction paragraph",
          "rule": "For square root extraction of a four-digit number: the main table contains roots of three-digit numbers between 1 and 100, calculated with four significant digits; a correction is taken on the fourth digit if present. Layout is described as like the preceding table."
        },
        {
          "id": "IV-addition",
          "source": "PDF40 / printed39 instruction examples",
          "rule": "The source explicitly ADDS corrections for fourth digits 6 (sqrt9.736) and 8 (sqrt36.48). This supports the n39 lesson's additive route even above 5; do not mechanically apply the III threshold."
        },
        {
          "id": "IV-subtraction-example",
          "source": "PDF40 / printed39 sqrt36.48 example",
          "rule": "The source also gives 6.042 minus correction on 2 equal to 2 as an alternative to 6.033 plus correction on 8 equal to 7. It does not print a universal IV rule requiring the next-main route above 5. One agreeing example is not proof that all rounded routes agree."
        },
        {
          "id": "IV-scale",
          "source": "PDF36-40 / printed35-39 footers and PDF40 scaling examples",
          "rule": "A decimal shift of 2,4,6,... places in N shifts the root by 1,2,3,... places in the same direction. Normalize positive radicands using an even power of ten, so the table coefficient lies between 1 and 100."
        },
        {
          "id": "IV-output-writing",
          "source": "PDF40 / printed39 final sentence",
          "rule": "Only the final result is written; this does not specify new intermediate-rounding precision."
        },
        {
          "id": "IV-over-resolution-and-guard",
